<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107184" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέρα</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ]</span>, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέρ</span>) an <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>upper rope</i>: mostly in pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέραι,</span> the <i>braces</i> attached to
			the ends of the sailyards (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίκρια</span>), by
			means of which the sails are shifted fore and aft, acc. to the
			direction of the wind, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				5.260
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DMort.</u>
				4.1
			</span></i>: prov. of those who drop the substance to grasp a shadow,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφεὶς τὴν ὑ. τὸν πόδα
			διώκει</span> he lets go <i>the brace</i> to catch at the
			sheet, <i><span class="en">
				Hyp.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				181
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέραι,</span>
			=
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕπερα, τά,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (s. v.l.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
